<title>SINGAPORE: SIMEX to consider contracts linked to Euro - TV.</title>
<headline>SIMEX to consider contracts linked to Euro - TV.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Singapore International Monetary Exchange (SIMEX) is looking at the possibility of listing futures and options based on the single European currency, state television said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It quoted SIMEX chairman Victor Liew as saying the exchange planned to broaden its range of contracts and explore links with other exchanges to remain competitive in the face of growing regional competition.</p>
<p>Total volume traded on SIMEX for the first 10 months of this year fell 10.9 percent to 19.2 million contracts from the same period last year, state television said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
